<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bertrand du Guesclin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1320–<a href="/years/1380">1380</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bertrand du Guesclin was a Breton knight who became constable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1370 and the leading French commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>. Captured at Auray in 1364 and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najera">Nájera</a> in 1367, he helped place <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile">Henry of Trastámara</a> on the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in 1369. Avoiding pitched battles, his campaigns of the 1370s recovered most of the lands ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. He was buried at Saint-Denis among the kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bertrand-du-guesclin.jpg" alt="Bertrand du Guesclin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Monniaux · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bertrand_du_Guesclin_P1210353.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
